  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A short checklist defines acceptable condition, and contributors remain at intake until any questions about their items have been resolved.\", \"decision\": \"How should contributed goods be checked before display?\", \"goal\": \"Help usable household goods reach interested neighbors while keeping contributions, claims, and final collection understandable.\", \"problem\": \"Neighbors are organizing a one-day fair for clean, usable household goods that people no longer need. Giving and taking are both optional, and no payment or matching contribution is required. Volunteers have intake space, category tables, reserve shelves, a holding area, carts, and simple item records. Contributors choose in advance whether unclaimed goods should be returned during the closing collection period or donated through an arranged pickup.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nContributors complete the condition checklist themselves, and intake volunteers review the answers while examining the listed concerns. The contributor’s knowledge directs attention to likely issues before volunteers decide whether the item is suitable for display.\nIntake volunteers inspect each contribution with the condition checklist while its contributor is present. Questions about damage or missing parts can be answered immediately before an item is accepted for display.\nOne volunteer asks contributors the condition-checklist questions while another examines their goods beside them. Conversation and inspection proceed together, allowing observed problems to be clarified before the contribution leaves the intake area."
    }
  ],
